+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+This contract defines the registry boundary between model-supplied input and tool execution.
+
+## Acceptance contract
+
+- `execute` validates required fields, declared types and enum constraints before invoking an executor, returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` on rejection, identifies property paths and constraints without exposing input values in results or logs, passes accepted input including unknown keys unchanged exactly once without coercion or defaults, and preserves the unknown-tool exception. ([validated by: rejects malformed tool input privately and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34))
+- `register` rejects an uncompilable static schema with the tool name in the error and compiles accepted static schemas at registration for reuse across ten executions. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L88))
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on every execution, validate using the current schema, and reuse compiled validators by resolved schema object identity. ([validated by: validates the current dynamic schema and caches each resolved schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L117))
+
+## Integration and release obligations
+
+The existing tool loop consumes rejection responses as ordinary tool results, allowing a corrected retry within its five-round budget; executor failures remain outside this input-validation contract.
+The implementation uses a JSON Schema validator in runtime dependencies, with no opt-out flag.
+README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md describe validation, extra-key preservation and rejection as a tool result; the execute comment is one line linking here.
+A MINOR release and consumer-facing changelog explain that executors no longer receive malformed inputs, including those they previously handled themselves.
diff --git a/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts
